"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Things to Take on a Trip"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you travel, you usually bring things that help you enjoy and remember the trip.<br />  Some examples are:<br /><br /> a waterproof camera (for trips near water)<br /> a change of clothes (for after swimming)<br /> sunglasses<br /> a hat<br /> a map<br /> a guidebook (a book that gives you information about a place or activity)<br /> a towel"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to Mexico for a vacation. I'm going to bring my waterproof camera and my sunglasses. <br/> They're going to Peru. They're going to take a guidebook and a map."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "waterproof camera "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a camera you can take into the water with you "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you taking your waterproof camera?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about travel."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "experienced "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having knowledge or skill in a particular subject "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's going to be an experienced guide."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a change of clothes "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of different clothes to put on after swimming "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you bring a change of clothes?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to kiss "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to touch with the lips  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you going to kiss the dolphins?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "at all times "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "always "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The guide is with us at all times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Plans and Intentions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the Present Continuous and Be Going To to talk about future actions and events. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You use the Present Continuous to talk about arrangements and plans. <br/> <br/>\"Be going to\" puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (decide to do something). <br/><br/>  Example: I'm going scuba diving. vs. I'm going to go scuba diving.  <br/>You can use \"intend to\" in place of \"be going to\". <br/> Example: I intend to go scuba diving tomorrow. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We are going to swim with dolphins tomorrow. <br/> We are swimming with dolphins at 3 p.m. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, imagine you are going on a trip to a sea mammal park where you can swim with dolphins."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Together, make a list of 5-10 things to take on your trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell another group what you have on your list."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare with them what are the same and what are different."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the differences with each other."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about intentions and plans."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about things to take on a trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list to organize things to bring."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about similarities and differences on my list."}]}], "type": "sena"}